## Step 1: Start with the given initial number of apples in the school cafeteria.
The school cafeteria initially had 38 apples.

## Step 2: Determine the number of apples remaining after using 20 to make lunch for the students.
The number of apples remaining after using 20 to make lunch for the students is 38 - 20 = 18.

## Step 3: Add the new number of apples purchased by the cafeteria to the remaining apples.
The school cafeteria then bought 28 more apples. So, we add 28 to the remaining 18 apples to get 18 + 28 = 46.

